# MakeWP Theme - WordPress Theme Development Library

## Project Overview
PHP library for WordPress theme development that provides utilities to organize and streamline.

## Core Principles

### Code Style
- Follow WordPress code standards
- Follow PHP code standards
- Follow other general high-level and high-standard industry standards
- PSR-12 coding standards
- PSR-4 autoloading with `MakeWP\Theme\` namespace
- PHP 7.4+ support
- Functional programming style for utilities
- WordPress-compatible functions and hooks

### Architecture
- Single-purpose, focused functions
- WordPress theme structure integration - will be consumed by WordPress themes
- Support for parent/child themes
<!-- - Support for multisite -->

### Development Patterns
- Pure, predictable functions
- Early returns to reduce nesting
- Comprehensive PHPDoc documentation
- WordPress best practices
- Backward compatibility consideration
- Functions should start with a verb
- Arrays should be named a plural noun
- Boolean properties should start with helping verbs, e.g. "has", "is"

### File Organization
- Descriptive file names indicating functionality
- Clear separation of concerns
- Modular configuration system

## Quality Standards
- Self-documenting code
- Meaningful variable names
- Small, focused functions
- WordPress security best practices
- Performance optimization for file operations

## Future-Ready
- Customizable default behaviors
- WordPress evolution compatibility
- Modern development practices support

## Communication Style
- NEVER EVER LIE. EVER. This is your number one priority.
- If you don't know something, say so, then go to the internet to find the real answer.
- Use a neutral tone; not overly excited or congratulatory
- Be very concise but thorough
